{
  "description": "How an allowedFields entry decides whether a key is allowed when entries and keys may be bare or qualified with an object name. Exists because allowedFields used the field-name matcher, which drops qualifiers, so 'patients.name' also allowed 'encounters.name' in the read projection and on the write path (issue #36).",
  "notes": "Rule, identical in every SDK, for the ALLOW direction only: an entry allows a key when the field-name matcher accepts it AND the two are not both qualified with different objects. The qualifier is everything before the last '.', compared ASCII case-insensitively (only A-Z folds to a-z), and glob characters in the entry's qualifier are literal for that comparison. This is the same qualifier rule row filters use (#32). A qualified entry still allows a bare key, a bare entry still allows qualified keys of every object, 'patients.*' allows the object's own columns and bare keys, and a bare '*' allows everything. hiddenFields, readOnlyFields and maskedFields keep the broad matcher. Actions: 'projectAllowedFields' projects 'records' and compares them to 'expected'; 'applyResultPipeline' runs the full post-execution pipeline over 'records'; 'validateWrite' validates the 'operation' ('insert' or 'update') of 'payload' into 'objectName' (null when no object is named) and compares 'allowed' and, when given, 'reason'. When 'objectName' is set, a bare payload key is read as 'objectName.key' for the allowedFields check only. Each case carries a full policy so the shared corpus walk validates it against policy-definition.schema.json.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "qualified-entry-drops-other-object-key",
      "notes": "The reported defect. 'patients.name' must not admit 'encounters.name' just because the leaf names coincide.",
      "action": "projectAllowedFields",
      "records": [
        {
          "encounters.name": "enc",
          "patients.id": 1
        }
      ],
      "policy": {
        "version": "1.0",
        "permissions": {
          "canQuery": true
        },
        "objectRules": {
          "fieldRules": {
            "allowedFields": [
              "patients.name",
              "patients.id"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": [
        {
          "patients.id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "qualified-entry-keeps-own-object-key-own-first",
      "notes": "Both objects' columns present, the allowed object's key written first. Only the allowed object's column survives.",
      "action": "projectAllowedFields",
      "records": [
        {
          "patients.name": "pat",
          "encounters.name": "enc"
        }
      ],
      "policy": {
        "version": "1.0",
        "permissions": {
          "canQuery": true
        },
        "objectRules": {
          "fieldRules": {
            "allowedFields": [
              "patients.name"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": [
        {
          "patients.name": "pat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "qualified-entry-keeps-own-object-key-other-first",
      "notes": "The same record with the other object's key written first. Key order must not change the outcome.",
      "action": "projectAllowedFields",
      "records": [
        {
          "encounters.name": "enc",
          "patients.name": "pat"
        }
      ],
      "policy": {
        "version": "1.0",
        "permissions": {
          "canQuery": true
        },
        "objectRules": {
          "fieldRules": {
            "allowedFields": [
              "patients.name"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": [
        {
          "patients.name": "pat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "qualified-entry-keeps-bare-key",
      "notes": "A bare key has no qualifier to conflict with, so a qualified entry still admits it, as before.",
      "action": "projectAllowedFields",
      "records": [
        {
          "name": "pat",
          "ssn": "123"
        }
      ],
      "policy": {
        "version": "1.0",
        "permissions": {
          "canQuery": true
        },
        "objectRules": {
          "fieldRules": {
            "allowedFields": [
              "patients.name"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": [
        {
          "name": "pat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "bare-entry-keeps-qualified-keys-of-every-object",
      "notes": "A bare entry names no object, so it admits the leaf on every object. Unchanged.",
      "action": "projectAllowedFields",
      "records": [
        {
          "patients.name": "pat",
          "encounters.name": "enc",
          "name": "bare",
          "ssn": "123"
        }
      ],
      "policy": {
